'''Jabba's Palace garage''', also referred to as the '''sail barge hangar''', was a [[hangar]] located underneath [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]]. The garage held Jabba's luxury [[sail barge]], the modified [[LO-KD57]] ''[[Khetanna]], ''as well as a number of [[Bantha-II cargo skiff]]s. After Jabba's death, the hangar held the ''[[Slave I]]'', until it was [[Firespray heist|recovered]] by [[Boba Fett]] and [[Fennec Shand]].

==Description and layout==
[[File:PalaceGarage.png|thumb|left|The garage underneath Jabba's Palace was where he housed his luxury sail barge ''Khetanna''|215x215px]]
The sail barge hangar was located underneath Jabba's Palace. Its primary access to the outside was a large hangar door, just outside of which were numerous junk piles made up of scrap metal. The main hangar was surrounded by a series of hallways and small rooms housing an assortment of amenities for the palace.<ref name="Battlefront" /> Above the hangar was a small watch tower, and a roadway located adjacent to the garage was circuitous to the city of [[Mos Eisley]] and provided an up-ramp for swoops housed in the garage. The floor of the hangar itself was made of polished stone, and on the ceiling was a ventilator. In addition to housing the ''Khetanna'', the garage served as a space for Jabba's many [[Bantha-II cargo skiff]]s and smaller vehicles to be stored, as well as the location of numerous workshops and animal pens.<ref name="CL" />

==History==
===Construction===
At some point after acquiring the former [[B'omarr Order|B'omarr]] monastery from the bandit [[Alkhara]] and transforming it into his palace, Jabba hired [[architect]] [[Derren Flet]] to modify the palace to suit his needs. This included the construction of the hangar to house Jabba's luxury sail barge ''Khetanna'', which Flet had commissioned from [[Ubrikkian Industries]]. Flet met his end when designing the palace dungeons, as he was executed by the Hutt for failing to deliver adequate holding for Jabba's many [[prisoner]]s.<ref name="CL" />

===Under Bib Fortuna===
By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="MandoDate">{{MandoDate|5}}</ref> [[Boba Fett]] was believed dead at the [[Rescue of Han Solo|skirmish]] at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]]. His ship, ''[[Slave I]]'', was kept in the hanger at the palace, now under the control of [[Bib Fortuna]]. Eventually, Fett and his new partner [[Fennec Shand]] [[Firespray heist|infiltrated]] the palace and retrieved his ship.<ref name="GatheringStorm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref>

===Under Boba Fett===
Fett later retrieved his armor and [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|attacked]] the palace. He killed Fortuna and took over the palace,<ref name="Chapter 16">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref> becoming the [[Daimyo]] of [[Mos Espa]].<ref name="Stranger">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref> Fennec Shand later recruited [[Din Djarin]] to serve as muscle in their [[War against the Pykes|war]] against the [[Pyke Syndicate]]. Djarin arrived at the garage and landed with his [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|N-1 starfighter]]. He was greeted by a [[Gamorrean]] guard and informed him that his presence was requested by Fennec Shand. Djarin joined a meeting with Fett's forces, and later left the hangar and traveled to [[Freetown]] to recruit [[Marshal]] [[Cobb Vanth]].<ref name="Chapter 6" />

